Fireball at unskilled or basic produces a 3x3 area blast, centred on
the point of impact. Cone of cold at same skill produces a ray of
cold. They're also very easy to use, because all you need to provide
is a valid direction, not a valid location (the latter requires
visibility, i.e. you might need to waste a turn making the target
location visible to you by casting a light spell or taking off a
blindfold).

> Actually, Basic causes the attack to hit nine squares, as it seems to be
> indended.  The difference with Skilled and higher is that there are
> multiple fireballs launched at the destination, making it very powerful.
> 
> In fact, I think it might be a bit too powerful... there's a big difference
> between Basic and Skilled, especially with doing 4x the damage on averag...

It has a _big_ drawback, though: you must cast skilled/expert
fireballs at a "valid" target - i.e. a place currently visible to you
and within "casting range". This makes them much more difficult to use
than "basic" in corridors, in Gehennom and on the astral plane, as
well as when engulfed or blind. I'd find it quite nice if there was
still the option to shoot your expert fireballs just giving a
direction, without the need to specify a target; in the current
incarnation, fireball and cone of cold are a lot safer and more
versatile at basic skill.

